Assistant: The error indicates that `HoverCardPortal` must be used within a `HoverCard` component. This is because `HoverCardPortal` is a compound component that relies on context from its parent `HoverCard` component. Let's fix this by wrapping the `HoverCardPortal` with the necessary `HoverCard` components.

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/HoverCardPortal-f32f8bfd.tsx">
  <change>
    <description>Wrap HoverCardPortal with HoverCard and add necessary components</description>
    <content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { 
  HoverCard,
  HoverCardContent, 
  HoverCardPortal,
  HoverCardTrigger 
} from '../../../../packages/ui/components/hover-card/index';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    className: {
      type: "string",
      value: "custom-class",
      label: "Class Name",
    },
    align: {
      type: "dropdown",
      value: "center",
      options: ["start", "center", "end"],
      label: "Alignment",
    },
    sideOffset: {
      type: "number",
      value: 4,
      label: "Side Offset",
    },
  });

  return (
    <HoverCard>
      <HoverCardTrigger asChild>
        <button>Hover me</button>
      </HoverCardTrigger>

      <HoverCardPortal>
        <HoverCardContent
          className={state.className.value}
          align={state.align.value}
          sideOffset={state.sideOffset.value}
        >
          <div>Hover Card Content</div>
        </HoverCardContent>
      </HoverCardPortal>
    </HoverCard>
  );
}
</content>
  </change>
</file>

I've made the following changes to fix the error:

1. Added imports for all necessary HoverCard components (`HoverCard`, `HoverCardContent`, `HoverCardTrigger`)
2. Wrapped the component with the root `HoverCard` component
3. Added `HoverCardTrigger` which is required to show/hide the hover card
4. Moved the props (className, align, sideOffset) to the `HoverCardContent` component where they belong
5. Properly structured the hover card with trigger and content components

This should resolve the context error and provide a working hover card implementation. The hover card will now appear when the user hovers over the trigger button.

